{"timestamp":"2026-06-14T15:28:54.335+05:30","incident_id":"inc-419aa91fdb","service":"auth-api","status":"APPROVED","severity":"CRITICAL","root_cause":"Most likely database timeout or connection contention affecting auth-api requests, with downstream auth failures; the data does not prove full connection-pool saturation.","ai_summary":"auth-api is showing elevated latency and intermittent authentication failures across both hosts and multiple regions. The strongest signal is database_timeout alongside response-time regression, but DB pool usage peaks below 70%, so this looks more like downstream database slowness or timeout propagation than hard pool exhaustion. Mixed dependency patterns (postgres, identity_provider, redis, payment_gateway) suggest verifying the database path first, then checking retry and pool behavior in the service.","remediation_status":"APPROVED","approved_by":"demo-operator","evidence_summary":"50 evidence events for auth-api across auth-01/auth-02; repeated auth_failure, database_timeout, and latency_regression signals; impacted endpoints include /login, /session, and /token/refresh; average latency 314.86 ms, max latency 2154 ms, max CPU 71.95%, max memory 74.93%, max DB pool 69.91%.","mcp_evidence_summary":"MCP client call: MCP evidence for auth-api: 50 events; errors=auth_failure, database_timeout, latency_regression; hosts=auth-01, auth-02; endpoints=/login, /session, /token/refresh; dependencies=identity_provider, none, payment_gateway, postgres; avg_latency_ms=315; max_latency_ms=2154; max_cpu_pct=72; max_db_pool_pct=70.","investigation_status":"APPROVED","mcp_investigation":true,"mcp_tools_used":["splunk_run_query"],"spl_queries_used":[],"mcp_log_event_count":50,"action":"remediation_approved","mode":"simulate","result":"Remediation approved by operator; execution pending.","sourcetype":"aiops-remediation"}
